    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508-a1">

                <pb facs="0630" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg528"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Japanese Patent
                            Office to Mr. E. F.
                    Crowe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of the 11th instant
                    I beg to say that Article XII of the Japanese trade-mark law is applicable only
                    to the case where business has been discontinued in which a registered
                    trade-mark was in use, but not to the case of nonuse of a registered trade-mark.
                    Nor is there any provision in the law by which a registered trade-mark can be
                    canceled on the ground that it has not been used, or on the ground that the
                    person who had had the trade-mark registered has not begun business at all.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morio Nakamatsu.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
